            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0607" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/7–348: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-07-03T13:00:00+09:00">July 3, 1948—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 3—2:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1221. ReDeptel 979, July 2, 7 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Re paragraph 2, impossible revise article V (see Embtel 1220, <pb
                            facs="0608" n="598" xml:id="pg598"/> July 3, 11 a.m.). To attempt to do
                        so would postpone signing after July 3.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Re paragraph 3: <list>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                            <item>Norm [<hi rendition="#italic">Term</hi>] “United States of
                                America” stricken from article IV;</item>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                            <item>Phrase cited at end second sentence, paragraph 1, article VI
                                missing from text. Further “objectives” appear our text.</item>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)</label>
                            <item>Paragraph 7 of annex not in text, but will be handled by exchange
                                of notes to be published.</item>
                        </list></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
